1
00:00:01,766 --> 00:00:04,495
(An Awesome Day)

2
00:00:04,496 --> 00:00:06,395
- Nice to see you. - Nice to see you.

3
00:00:06,396 --> 00:00:07,765
All right.

4
00:00:07,766 --> 00:00:10,306
The guest for today's Rainbow Live is...

5
00:00:10,566 --> 00:00:13,006
a distinguished individual on a global scale.

6
00:00:13,836 --> 00:00:15,505
- Didn't he win an award? - He did.

7
00:00:15,506 --> 00:00:16,775
- He won the Gold Glove Award. - He's...

8
00:00:16,776 --> 00:00:17,776
- Yes. - the first Korean to win it.

9
00:00:17,777 --> 00:00:18,945
- The 1st Asian player to win it. - The 1st Asian player to win it.

10
00:00:18,946 --> 00:00:20,045
- The Gold Glove Award for Utility. - Yes.

11
00:00:20,046 --> 00:00:21,175
It means he's the best defensive player...

12
00:00:21,176 --> 00:00:22,815
- in the US. - Right.

13
00:00:22,816 --> 00:00:25,015
Is that equivalent to winning the Ballon d'Or?

14
00:00:25,016 --> 00:00:26,456
- Yes. - That's it.

15
00:00:26,856 --> 00:00:30,126
And he rarely stars on variety shows, right?

16
00:00:30,256 --> 00:00:31,395
- He rarely does. - Right.

17
00:00:31,396 --> 00:00:33,826
Did you believe it when you heard he'd be on the show?

18
00:00:33,896 --> 00:00:38,135
He's my favorite baseball player.

19
00:00:38,136 --> 00:00:41,606
I bet baseball fans have been waiting for this day.

20
00:00:42,936 --> 00:00:44,705
All right. He's the first Korean MLB player...

21
00:00:44,706 --> 00:00:46,576
to win the Gold Glove Award.

22
00:00:46,836 --> 00:00:48,345
He's a world-class shortstop.

23
00:00:48,346 --> 00:00:49,976
It's Awesome Kim, Kim Ha Seong.

24
00:00:50,876 --> 00:00:51,916
For real?

25
00:00:54,616 --> 00:00:58,055
(Kim Ha Seong shows up.)

26
00:00:58,056 --> 00:00:59,116
This feels surreal.

27
00:01:01,633 --> 00:01:03,562
(In 2019, he scored the most runs in the KBO league.)

28
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:05,433
(He won the Golden Glove Award 3 years in a row since 2018.)

29
00:01:06,033 --> 00:01:08,333
(He also excelled as the national team's starting shortstop.)

30
00:01:09,733 --> 00:01:11,402
(2017: Silver medal from the Asia Professional Baseball Championship)

31
00:01:11,403 --> 00:01:12,842
(2018: Golden Glove Award from the KBO, gold medal)

32
00:01:12,843 --> 00:01:14,342
(2019: The most runs in the KBO, the Best Batter of the Year,)

33
00:01:14,343 --> 00:01:15,913
(Golden Glove Award from the KBO, runner-up in the WBSC Premier12)

34
00:01:16,873 --> 00:01:17,883
(Afterward, he joined the MLB.)

35
00:01:18,413 --> 00:01:20,043
(He proved his talent by making a strong impression.)

36
00:01:20,713 --> 00:01:23,513
(He proudly earned his place among the league's top players.)

37
00:01:24,283 --> 00:01:25,452
(The first Korean player...)

38
00:01:25,453 --> 00:01:26,683
(to win the Gold Glove Award in the MLB.)

39
00:01:27,453 --> 00:01:29,293
(Baseball Player Kim Ha Seong)

40
00:01:29,993 --> 00:01:33,323
(We welcome you from the bottom of our heart.)

41
00:01:33,563 --> 00:01:34,962
- This feels surreal. - My gosh. Hello.

42
00:01:34,963 --> 00:01:35,963
Hello.

43
00:01:35,964 --> 00:01:37,032
(Catch my ball.)

44
00:01:37,033 --> 00:01:38,432
- Hey. - Come to the center. Hello.

45
00:01:38,433 --> 00:01:40,303
- Please come to the center. - It's like I'm dreaming.

46
00:01:40,863 --> 00:01:42,073
This feels surreal.

47
00:01:42,673 --> 00:01:44,702
All right. Say hello to our viewers first.

48
00:01:44,703 --> 00:01:45,703
Okay.

49
00:01:45,704 --> 00:01:48,113
Hello. I'm a baseball player. My name is Kim Ha Seong.

50
00:01:48,973 --> 00:01:50,043
Why...

51
00:01:50,613 --> 00:01:52,283
- Are you that nervous? - No.

52
00:01:53,083 --> 00:01:54,913
(Nervously shifting his gaze)

53
00:01:55,383 --> 00:01:56,612
He's an extrovert.

54
00:01:56,613 --> 00:01:58,152
But from what I know, he's just shy in the beginning.

55
00:01:58,153 --> 00:01:59,352
- Oh, he is? - Yes.

56
00:01:59,353 --> 00:02:00,723
(Thank you.)

57
00:02:00,883 --> 00:02:02,393
It's your first time meeting all of us, right?

58
00:02:02,523 --> 00:02:04,192
Yes. I've only seen you on TV.

59
00:02:04,193 --> 00:02:06,123
How does it feel to be in the presence of superstars?

60
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:08,693
(Trailing off)

61
00:02:09,063 --> 00:02:10,733
It feels surreal. It's like I'm watching TV.

62
00:02:10,993 --> 00:02:12,732
(How cute.)

63
00:02:12,733 --> 00:02:14,262
I'd like to ask you how it feels to be here...

64
00:02:14,263 --> 00:02:15,633
for the first time.

65
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:19,273
Well, I think it's a bit small.

66
00:02:20,943 --> 00:02:23,312
- Compared to what you saw on TV? - Yes. The studio...

67
00:02:23,313 --> 00:02:26,512
- It's smaller than the MLB. - No.

68
00:02:26,513 --> 00:02:28,452
Our studio is too small to host a superstar.

69
00:02:28,453 --> 00:02:29,552
Gosh, no.

70
00:02:29,553 --> 00:02:31,852
By the way, I really wanted to meet you.

71
00:02:31,853 --> 00:02:33,183
- Can I shake your hand? - Sure.

72
00:02:33,623 --> 00:02:35,753
You have such big hands.

73
00:02:36,393 --> 00:02:37,892
- Look at that. - Your hands are so big.

74
00:02:37,893 --> 00:02:39,093
- Can I compare our hands? - Your hand...

75
00:02:39,363 --> 00:02:40,363
(Everyone wants to compare their hands.)

76
00:02:40,364 --> 00:02:41,693
His fingers are a joint longer than mine.

77
00:02:41,893 --> 00:02:43,063
- He has big hands. - His hands are so big.

78
00:02:43,593 --> 00:02:44,702
My left hand...

79
00:02:44,703 --> 00:02:45,832
(Shy)

80
00:02:45,833 --> 00:02:49,173
- I hear you're a free agent now. - Yes.

81
00:02:49,573 --> 00:02:52,442
They're discussing 70 million dollars...

82
00:02:52,443 --> 00:02:53,873
for your annual salary.

83
00:02:54,243 --> 00:02:56,613
So you can join any team now, right?

84
00:02:56,943 --> 00:03:00,343
I just know that my agent is working hard.

85
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:02,353
Is there a team you want to join?

86
00:03:02,753 --> 00:03:03,952
- San Francisco? - No comment.

87
00:03:03,953 --> 00:03:05,953
- Isn't that a sensitive question? - Is it?

88
00:03:06,623 --> 00:03:08,493
Well, he doesn't have to answer it.

89
00:03:08,893 --> 00:03:10,693
I'm going to ask him how much money he has.

90
00:03:11,053 --> 00:03:12,222
- Okay. - Do you think you can answer that?

91
00:03:12,223 --> 00:03:13,623
- Yes. - Okay.

92
00:03:13,963 --> 00:03:15,932
All right. Now that you're in the Rainbow family,

93
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:17,132
once you make your decision,

94
00:03:17,133 --> 00:03:18,732
you must tell us first. Okay?

95
00:03:18,733 --> 00:03:19,803
- Sure. - Okay.

96
00:03:20,203 --> 00:03:21,573
- Really? - You'll tell us first?

97
00:03:21,933 --> 00:03:23,403
(Chuckling)

98
00:03:23,773 --> 00:03:26,842
- Could you sign my uniform later? - Sure.

99
00:03:26,843 --> 00:03:28,243
- He'll take pictures too. - Please sign it.

100
00:03:28,643 --> 00:03:29,772
I must post it on my social media.

101
00:03:29,773 --> 00:03:31,682
(He'll go on Moomoo's social media which only features superstars.)

102
00:03:31,683 --> 00:03:34,612
All right. Let's check out the day-to-day life of Kim Ha Seong,

103
00:03:34,613 --> 00:03:36,052
the MLB player.

104
00:03:36,053 --> 00:03:38,423
(Let's check it out.)

105
00:03:39,323 --> 00:03:40,752
(A Major Day)

106
00:03:40,753 --> 00:03:41,923
- "A Major Day." - "A Major Day."

107
00:03:45,793 --> 00:03:46,892
(Squirming)

108
00:03:46,893 --> 00:03:48,433
Your house is really dark.

109
00:03:51,563 --> 00:03:53,003
Gosh, the angle of your hand...

110
00:03:53,803 --> 00:03:54,932
- He's throwing a ball. - That's...

111
00:03:54,933 --> 00:03:56,432
- His forearm muscles are trained. - Yes.

112
00:03:56,433 --> 00:03:58,203
- That's the throwing pose. - Right.

113
00:04:04,073 --> 00:04:06,112
It's strange. I can't stop looking at his hand.

114
00:04:06,113 --> 00:04:07,142
- Right. - Of course.

115
00:04:07,143 --> 00:04:08,182
Right.

116
00:04:08,183 --> 00:04:10,453
(Blinking)

117
00:04:13,323 --> 00:04:17,823
(I should get up.)

118
00:04:23,733 --> 00:04:29,233
(He makes the bed as soon as he wakes up.)

119
00:04:38,113 --> 00:04:40,443
Hello. I'm a baseball player, Kim Ha Seong.

120
00:04:41,413 --> 00:04:43,413
- He's so handsome. - Gosh, look at the trophy.

121
00:04:44,413 --> 00:04:46,923
(He drinks water as soon as he gets up.)

122
00:04:48,493 --> 00:04:50,553
I'm curious about the house of an MLB player.

123
00:04:50,793 --> 00:04:52,062
You know what I'm curious about?

124
00:04:52,063 --> 00:04:53,863
I'm curious if he can toss the trash...

125
00:04:53,963 --> 00:04:56,362
- into the bin in one go. - If he can make it in one go.

126
00:04:56,363 --> 00:04:57,492
- He must have good aim. - Because he throws baseballs?

127
00:04:57,493 --> 00:04:58,533
He throws baseballs.

128
00:04:58,803 --> 00:05:01,103
- I just put it in the bin. - Are you good at that?

129
00:05:01,303 --> 00:05:02,533
- I don't throw it. - I see.

130
00:05:03,003 --> 00:05:04,772
See? He just puts it in the bin.

131
00:05:04,773 --> 00:05:06,002
You must at least throw your socks...

132
00:05:06,003 --> 00:05:07,272
- into the laundry hamper. - Right.

133
00:05:07,273 --> 00:05:08,573
- Well... - What about your socks?

134
00:05:08,843 --> 00:05:11,343
I take a shower after my games in the US.

135
00:05:11,513 --> 00:05:12,942
The laundry hamper is quite big.

136
00:05:12,943 --> 00:05:15,082
Then I take off my uniform and toss it in the hamper.

137
00:05:15,083 --> 00:05:16,282
- Do they go in then? - They go in, right?

138
00:05:16,283 --> 00:05:17,313
They go in almost every time.

139
00:05:17,513 --> 00:05:18,722
- That's good. - What if you toss them,

140
00:05:18,723 --> 00:05:19,922
and they don't go in?

141
00:05:19,923 --> 00:05:21,452
- What do you do? - I walk over and put them in.

142
00:05:21,453 --> 00:05:22,552
You walk over and put them in?

143
00:05:22,553 --> 00:05:23,653
He'll pick them up.

144
00:05:23,823 --> 00:05:24,823
(Chuckling)

145
00:05:26,663 --> 00:05:28,493
(He plops down with a remote.)

146
00:05:28,963 --> 00:05:30,433
(Clicking)

147
00:05:34,303 --> 00:05:35,633
- What? - Is it automatic?

148
00:05:35,933 --> 00:05:37,033
- What? - What's this?

149
00:05:39,503 --> 00:05:40,772
The skyscraper in Jamsil, L Tower.

150
00:05:40,773 --> 00:05:42,213
- L Tower. - That's Seokchon Lake.

151
00:05:43,113 --> 00:05:46,683
I've been playing baseball in the US for five years.

152
00:05:46,913 --> 00:05:48,553
Whenever I come back to Seoul,

153
00:05:48,613 --> 00:05:52,123
I stay here for about three months during the off-season.

154
00:05:55,144 --> 00:05:56,273
That's so tall.

155
00:05:56,274 --> 00:05:57,774
I get a panoramic view of Seoul.

156
00:05:57,944 --> 00:06:00,244
It overlooks Lotte World and Seokchon Lake too.

157
00:06:00,744 --> 00:06:02,454
I do stay in the US longer,

158
00:06:02,584 --> 00:06:05,754
but Korea feels more like home to me.

159
00:06:06,024 --> 00:06:09,354
I spent more time decorating my house in Korea.

160
00:06:12,294 --> 00:06:14,493
- What a beautiful home. - You got a great home.

161
00:06:14,494 --> 00:06:15,563
It's so neat.

162
00:06:15,564 --> 00:06:16,634
(The sweet home of an MLB player)

163
00:06:22,174 --> 00:06:23,274
How neat.

164
00:06:23,634 --> 00:06:25,034
You're so tidy.

165
00:06:25,474 --> 00:06:27,144
Gosh, your house is really neat.

166
00:06:29,514 --> 00:06:31,544
(Then there's an open view of Seokchon Lake.)

167
00:06:32,914 --> 00:06:34,983
You've kept the uniform for every team you played for.

168
00:06:34,984 --> 00:06:36,054
Yes.

169
00:06:37,484 --> 00:06:39,383
- They're Korean awards. - Yes.

170
00:06:39,384 --> 00:06:40,584
- I won them in Korea. - How fascinating.

171
00:06:42,094 --> 00:06:44,553
(His collection of trophies proves his talent.)

172
00:06:44,554 --> 00:06:46,023
Gosh, he won so many awards.

173
00:06:46,024 --> 00:06:47,024
(His collection of trophies proves his talent.)

174
00:06:47,809 --> 00:06:51,079
(Fancy)

175
00:06:51,309 --> 00:06:53,048
(My first hit as a professional player)

176
00:06:53,049 --> 00:06:54,208
What are these baseballs?

177
00:06:54,209 --> 00:06:56,919
Whenever I hit a meaningful milestone,

178
00:06:57,319 --> 00:06:58,888
- my team gives me the ball. - I see. It's written on the ball.

179
00:06:58,889 --> 00:07:00,418
"My first home run as a professional player."

180
00:07:00,419 --> 00:07:01,588
So that's the ball...

181
00:07:01,589 --> 00:07:02,718
- you hit your first home run with. - Yes.

182
00:07:02,719 --> 00:07:04,588
- The ball went over the fence. - How did you get that back?

183
00:07:04,589 --> 00:07:05,688
Did they take it from the fan?

184
00:07:05,689 --> 00:07:07,488
For meaningful milestones...

185
00:07:07,489 --> 00:07:08,628
- like the first home run, - The fans usually return it.

186
00:07:08,629 --> 00:07:10,798
- the fans... Yes. - Do they return the ball?

187
00:07:10,799 --> 00:07:12,468
We give them a signed bat instead.

188
00:07:12,469 --> 00:07:14,168
- I see. You exchange them? - We trade them.

189
00:07:14,169 --> 00:07:15,169
(They exchange the ball with the signed bat.)

190
00:07:15,170 --> 00:07:17,299
Fans usually return the balls.

191
00:07:18,269 --> 00:07:19,538
(On one corner, there's the Gold Glove from the MLB.)

192
00:07:19,539 --> 00:07:21,469
- That's the one from the US. - Yes.

193
00:07:21,639 --> 00:07:22,808
That's his pride.

194
00:07:22,809 --> 00:07:24,408
Kim Ha Seong from San Diego...

195
00:07:24,409 --> 00:07:25,978
("Kim Ha Seong, First Korean to win the Gold Glove in the MLB")

196
00:07:25,979 --> 00:07:27,648
("Kim Ha Seong Makes MLB History")

197
00:07:27,649 --> 00:07:29,348
("First Asian Shortstop in the MLB to Win Gold Glove")

198
00:07:29,349 --> 00:07:30,349
The Gold Glove.

199
00:07:30,350 --> 00:07:31,789
- He's the 1st Asian player. - He's the 1st Asian player.

200
00:07:32,319 --> 00:07:36,619
(Only the Gold Glove winners can have...)

201
00:07:37,559 --> 00:07:38,588
(this gold patch.)

202
00:07:38,589 --> 00:07:39,689
That's so cool.

203
00:07:40,259 --> 00:07:42,498
He didn't win the Gold Glove as a shortstop.

204
00:07:42,499 --> 00:07:43,898
- He won the Gold Glove for Utility. - For Utility.

205
00:07:43,899 --> 00:07:45,628
- He can play any position. - I see.

206
00:07:45,629 --> 00:07:46,728
- He's multi-talented. - He won the award...

207
00:07:46,729 --> 00:07:47,868
- Yes. - for having many talents.

208
00:07:47,869 --> 00:07:48,998
- Being a shortstop is one of them. - Right.

209
00:07:48,999 --> 00:07:50,269
- My gosh. - An award for having many talents?

210
00:07:50,369 --> 00:07:51,769
I used to play shortstop primarily.

211
00:07:52,369 --> 00:07:54,338
But once I went to the US,

212
00:07:54,339 --> 00:07:56,308
I started to play multiple positions.

213
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:58,909
So you can play all the infield positions, right?

214
00:07:59,009 --> 00:08:00,349
And his batting score was good too.

215
00:08:00,679 --> 00:08:02,118
He's a great shortstop.

216
00:08:02,119 --> 00:08:03,378
- And he's a good batter too. - He's a defensive player...

217
00:08:03,379 --> 00:08:04,619
- who scores too. - Right.

218
00:08:04,644 --> 00:08:05,854
- That's right. - Yes.

219
00:08:05,896 --> 00:08:07,136
What's this gold patch?

220
00:08:07,396 --> 00:08:09,535
Only the Gold Glove winners get this patch.

221
00:08:09,536 --> 00:08:11,336
It's from Rawlings.

222
00:08:11,736 --> 00:08:13,706
- It's like getting a star. - The winners get a patch.

223
00:08:14,336 --> 00:08:17,645
- Only the winners can wear it? - Yes, only the winners can wear it.

224
00:08:17,646 --> 00:08:20,446
- That's the pride. - I wanted to get his autograph,

225
00:08:20,616 --> 00:08:22,986
so I looked up the glove from that brand to buy it.

226
00:08:23,246 --> 00:08:24,915
- It was so expensive. - Really?

227
00:08:24,916 --> 00:08:27,756
- But it's leather. - It's so expensive.

228
00:08:27,816 --> 00:08:29,726
Is there one with faux leather, not real leather?

229
00:08:30,956 --> 00:08:32,055
- Well, - Now...

230
00:08:32,056 --> 00:08:34,555
there must be one with faux leather.

231
00:08:34,556 --> 00:08:36,025
We should implement...

232
00:08:36,026 --> 00:08:37,495
- the three-strike rule. - Right now...

233
00:08:37,496 --> 00:08:38,966
- One strike. - Two fouls.

234
00:08:38,996 --> 00:08:40,336
Is there one with faux leather, not real leather?

235
00:08:40,396 --> 00:08:42,636
- Two fouls. - You said it was expensive.

236
00:08:42,766 --> 00:08:43,936
Two fouls.

237
00:08:49,276 --> 00:08:50,346
What's this sound?

238
00:08:50,806 --> 00:08:51,876
Is that Latin music?

239
00:08:53,316 --> 00:08:56,686
(He plays Latin music in the house.)

240
00:08:58,186 --> 00:09:00,686
(Beating)

241
00:09:01,756 --> 00:09:05,126
When I wake up, I like to listen to Latin music.

242
00:09:05,286 --> 00:09:08,496
After I got to MLB, I met a lot of Latin American players.

243
00:09:08,626 --> 00:09:10,866
Jurickson Profar.

244
00:09:10,966 --> 00:09:13,266
- Fernando Tatis. And Machado. - Tatis.

245
00:09:13,466 --> 00:09:14,836
I'm close to everyone.

246
00:09:14,966 --> 00:09:18,236
There was always Latin music in the clubhouse.

247
00:09:18,406 --> 00:09:20,036
I didn't understand the lyrics.

248
00:09:20,236 --> 00:09:24,145
But Latin music just puts me in a good mood.

249
00:09:24,146 --> 00:09:25,676
It lifts my mood.

250
00:09:26,846 --> 00:09:28,516
Latin music is upbeat too.

251
00:09:29,686 --> 00:09:31,516
(Rummaging through)

252
00:09:32,816 --> 00:09:34,215
(The fridge is well-organized too.)

253
00:09:34,216 --> 00:09:35,985
- It's so neat. - It's well-organized.

254
00:09:35,986 --> 00:09:37,156
Gosh, what's this?

255
00:09:38,556 --> 00:09:40,055
(There are many side dishes too.)

256
00:09:40,056 --> 00:09:41,456
