517
00:21:15,656 --> 00:21:17,726
(He suddenly takes off his shirt.)

518
00:21:18,356 --> 00:21:19,525
He should take it off.

519
00:21:19,526 --> 00:21:20,726
(Now that he takes off a layer of shirt,)

520
00:21:22,196 --> 00:21:23,365
(he moves onto a rotating warm-up with a kettlebell.)

521
00:21:23,366 --> 00:21:25,125
- His arms look great. - Ten each.

522
00:21:25,126 --> 00:21:26,296
Gosh, look at his arms.

523
00:21:26,836 --> 00:21:27,836
Check out his core stability.

524
00:21:27,837 --> 00:21:30,266
That's it. Men must have thick arms.

525
00:21:31,666 --> 00:21:34,036
(These muscles are hard-earned.)

526
00:21:34,806 --> 00:21:35,836
Two.

527
00:21:36,136 --> 00:21:37,275
His forearm muscles...

528
00:21:37,276 --> 00:21:38,806
- are no joke. - Seriously.

529
00:21:40,616 --> 00:21:41,745
Once people see how fit you've become,

530
00:21:41,746 --> 00:21:44,886
they'll say that you've bulked up.

531
00:21:46,546 --> 00:21:50,386
Because I was very skinny in my younger days,

532
00:21:51,056 --> 00:21:52,585
I lacked strength.

533
00:21:52,586 --> 00:21:54,325
- He was different. - He was skin and bones.

534
00:21:54,326 --> 00:21:55,695
- He was so skinny. - So...

535
00:21:55,696 --> 00:21:56,795
(Ha Seong had a small frame in the past.)

536
00:21:56,796 --> 00:21:59,466
With hopes to become stronger,

537
00:21:59,596 --> 00:22:01,166
I bulked up.

538
00:22:02,166 --> 00:22:04,766
(This is how he looks now.)

539
00:22:05,106 --> 00:22:06,776
How much weight did you put on?

540
00:22:07,236 --> 00:22:10,405
I weighed 68kg when I joined the team.

541
00:22:10,406 --> 00:22:11,675
- You were so skinny. - Did you say 68kg?

542
00:22:11,676 --> 00:22:13,475
- I was 20 years old. - His nickname was Thorn.

543
00:22:13,476 --> 00:22:15,145
I wanted to become...

544
00:22:15,146 --> 00:22:17,215
a shortstop who could hit home runs.

545
00:22:17,216 --> 00:22:20,486
Now, I weigh about 90kg.

546
00:22:21,156 --> 00:22:24,126
- You gained over 20kg. - You gained over 20kg.

547
00:22:24,326 --> 00:22:27,155
I'm trying to maintain the weight...

548
00:22:27,156 --> 00:22:29,756
- that gave me the best performance. - You're trying to maintain it.

549
00:22:29,956 --> 00:22:32,095
It's extremely hard for skinny people to bulk up.

550
00:22:32,096 --> 00:22:33,566
- I heard that it was hard. - It's hard.

551
00:22:35,636 --> 00:22:37,166
He put in a lot of effort.

552
00:22:39,866 --> 00:22:41,375
- His body is full of power. - That's right.

553
00:22:41,376 --> 00:22:42,736
(His forearm muscles are working hard.)

554
00:22:43,746 --> 00:22:45,706
(He wraps up the warmup.)

555
00:22:47,476 --> 00:22:49,616
The warmup is over.

556
00:22:50,546 --> 00:22:52,845
(The training begins in earnest.)

557
00:22:52,846 --> 00:22:54,786
- What? - I haven't seen...

558
00:22:55,086 --> 00:22:56,216
that exercise machine before.

559
00:22:56,802 --> 00:22:59,031
(The training begins in earnest.)

560
00:22:59,032 --> 00:23:00,902
- What? - I haven't seen...

561
00:23:01,302 --> 00:23:02,401
that exercise machine before.

562
00:23:02,402 --> 00:23:04,441
It'd be best for you to make the movements...

563
00:23:04,442 --> 00:23:06,572
- that suit your technique. - Is that for pulling?

564
00:23:07,112 --> 00:23:10,211
(He swings it.)

565
00:23:10,212 --> 00:23:12,112
- I see that it's for batting. - Three.

566
00:23:12,912 --> 00:23:15,321
(The movement is similar to batting.)

567
00:23:15,322 --> 00:23:16,552
It's similar.

568
00:23:16,952 --> 00:23:17,992
Five.

569
00:23:18,892 --> 00:23:21,962
The momentary power and speed are important...

570
00:23:22,492 --> 00:23:24,562
in baseball.

571
00:23:25,062 --> 00:23:26,731
So I use weight...

572
00:23:26,732 --> 00:23:29,202
that's heavier than a bat to practice rotation.

573
00:23:29,432 --> 00:23:31,071
- One. - It must be so hard.

574
00:23:31,072 --> 00:23:32,832
Two. Okay.

575
00:23:33,182 --> 00:23:35,152
- What's that? - What's that?

576
00:23:35,952 --> 00:23:38,652
(He throws a ball that's heavier than a bat to practice rotation.)

577
00:23:39,222 --> 00:23:40,991
- Is that the same training? - Yes.

578
00:23:40,992 --> 00:23:42,822
It's for the core and rotation.

579
00:23:43,722 --> 00:23:46,331
(This time, he throws the ball downward!)

580
00:23:46,332 --> 00:23:47,562
He has so much strength.

581
00:23:47,862 --> 00:23:50,062
(Pounding)

582
00:23:50,432 --> 00:23:51,462
Okay.

583
00:23:51,562 --> 00:23:53,932
I'm reminded of what we did.

584
00:23:54,272 --> 00:23:55,372
- Volleyball? - Volleyball.

585
00:23:56,102 --> 00:23:59,412
(They're reminded of the match they had on a rainy day.)

586
00:24:00,312 --> 00:24:02,011
Why were you reminded of that?

587
00:24:02,012 --> 00:24:03,882
- It wasn't similar at all. - Volleyball.

588
00:24:04,342 --> 00:24:05,351
One.

589
00:24:05,352 --> 00:24:07,112
- I hope he comes to the event. - Two.

590
00:24:08,052 --> 00:24:09,052
Three.

591
00:24:09,552 --> 00:24:11,382
- He doesn't get exhausted. - Okay.

592
00:24:11,522 --> 00:24:12,792
It must be because he has good stamina.

593
00:24:13,652 --> 00:24:16,222
How does the training feel?

594
00:24:16,822 --> 00:24:19,132
- It's easy. - "It's easy."

595
00:24:19,632 --> 00:24:21,532
You don't need to do the shoulder exercise...

596
00:24:21,692 --> 00:24:23,101
as often as you did...

597
00:24:23,102 --> 00:24:24,332
during rehabilitation.

598
00:24:25,002 --> 00:24:26,932
You just need to do it lightly once or twice a week.

599
00:24:27,472 --> 00:24:31,172
When I was in San Diego last August,

600
00:24:31,542 --> 00:24:32,842
my shoulder got dislocated.

601
00:24:34,312 --> 00:24:36,512
My shoulder got dislocated during a slide.

602
00:24:38,282 --> 00:24:40,882
I ended up getting surgery.

603
00:24:40,982 --> 00:24:42,782
- Oh, no. - That's insane.

604
00:24:43,582 --> 00:24:46,422
You got injured when your performance was top-notch.

605
00:24:46,822 --> 00:24:49,922
Some people were saying that your career might end...

606
00:24:50,092 --> 00:24:51,392
because the injury was so big.

607
00:24:51,592 --> 00:24:52,832
How did you feel back then?

608
00:24:54,532 --> 00:24:56,332
I wasn't in my right mind.

609
00:24:56,462 --> 00:24:59,132
I bet you wondered if it was the end for you.

610
00:24:59,432 --> 00:25:02,672
I didn't think that.

611
00:25:03,442 --> 00:25:04,672
I didn't think that.

612
00:25:05,172 --> 00:25:06,272
Foul.

613
00:25:06,542 --> 00:25:08,141
- What? - Foul.

614
00:25:08,142 --> 00:25:09,942
- Foul. - Was it your first foul?

615
00:25:10,512 --> 00:25:12,712
- Back then, I thought I was okay. - Really?

616
00:25:13,252 --> 00:25:14,782
I did a lot of physical therapy,

617
00:25:15,182 --> 00:25:18,281
but I ended up getting surgery.

618
00:25:18,282 --> 00:25:20,092
It was very hard on me.

619
00:25:20,392 --> 00:25:23,261
A shoulder surgery is the biggest deal...

620
00:25:23,262 --> 00:25:24,922
for baseball players.

621
00:25:25,092 --> 00:25:27,961
During rehabilitation, I wondered if I'd be able to return...

622
00:25:27,962 --> 00:25:30,062
and give the same performance...

623
00:25:30,202 --> 00:25:31,662
as I did in the past.

624
00:25:31,832 --> 00:25:33,672
I had a lot of anxiety.

625
00:25:34,502 --> 00:25:36,842
- But I'm in great shape now. - Thank goodness.

626
00:25:37,042 --> 00:25:38,872
It isn't much of physical therapy...

627
00:25:39,272 --> 00:25:41,882
but training for next season.

628
00:25:42,312 --> 00:25:43,781
I'm so thankful...

629
00:25:43,782 --> 00:25:45,281
- that your shoulders got better. - I know.

630
00:25:45,282 --> 00:25:46,481
- Yes. - It's the best news...

631
00:25:46,482 --> 00:25:48,111
for the fans.

632
00:25:48,112 --> 00:25:49,482
Your shoulders are back to normal.

633
00:25:50,052 --> 00:25:51,421
(He puts on new equipment for his shoulders.)

634
00:25:51,422 --> 00:25:52,622
A bit up.

635
00:25:54,252 --> 00:25:55,422
What's that?

636
00:25:55,962 --> 00:25:57,122
What could that be?

637
00:26:01,032 --> 00:26:03,401
When you tighten it, it limits the blood flow.

638
00:26:03,402 --> 00:26:05,901
(It's equipment that limits the blood flow.)

639
00:26:05,902 --> 00:26:07,871
It stresses the muscles...

640
00:26:07,872 --> 00:26:09,402
and increases the blood flow in the arms.

641
00:26:10,242 --> 00:26:12,111
It strengthens the shoulders.

642
00:26:12,112 --> 00:26:13,241
(It increases the efficiency of a light exercise.)

643
00:26:13,242 --> 00:26:15,211
- How many have I done? - His arms turned red.

644
00:26:15,212 --> 00:26:16,682
You're right. They turned red.

645
00:26:16,982 --> 00:26:18,242
How fascinating.

646
00:26:20,082 --> 00:26:21,412
There are all sorts of devices.

647
00:26:21,782 --> 00:26:23,782
The pressure must be great.

648
00:26:26,592 --> 00:26:28,122
- Why is he getting dragged? - He's exhausted.

649
00:26:28,452 --> 00:26:30,022
Why are you coming toward me?

650
00:26:30,722 --> 00:26:31,722
(Inching)

651
00:26:31,723 --> 00:26:32,861
- Little by little... - Step back.

652
00:26:32,862 --> 00:26:34,891
(The major league uses a trick.)

653
00:26:34,892 --> 00:26:36,531
It's my first time seeing him struggle.

654
00:26:36,532 --> 00:26:37,602
- It's my first time. - Yes.

655
00:26:38,202 --> 00:26:39,431
- It must be refreshing. - The blood will flow.

656
00:26:39,432 --> 00:26:41,531
- The blood will flow now. - Yes.

657
00:26:41,532 --> 00:26:43,402
- It feels nice. - When your blood flows.

658
00:26:45,772 --> 00:26:46,912
Is there more?

659
00:26:47,772 --> 00:26:48,812
It's 20kg.

660
00:26:49,582 --> 00:26:51,642
One. Two.

661
00:26:52,052 --> 00:26:54,112
- What? - Is he doing that with 20kg?

662
00:26:54,752 --> 00:26:56,521
Does that vest weigh 20kg?

663
00:26:56,522 --> 00:26:57,782
It's a weighted vest.

664
00:26:59,922 --> 00:27:01,792
He exercises while wearing that vest.

665
00:27:02,462 --> 00:27:04,692
(His muscles bulge.)

666
00:27:05,892 --> 00:27:07,561
(A rubber band in one hand...)

667
00:27:07,562 --> 00:27:09,232
(and an 8kg kettlebell in another)

668
00:27:10,402 --> 00:27:12,031
His shoulders look totally fine...

669
00:27:12,032 --> 00:27:13,732
even in the eyes of non-experts like us.

670
00:27:14,272 --> 00:27:16,171
How does he not grimace?

671
00:27:16,172 --> 00:27:18,502
Seriously. His facial expression doesn't change.

672
00:27:19,712 --> 00:27:21,441
(Even during the off-season, he doesn't stop training.)

673
00:27:21,442 --> 00:27:22,912
Three. A bit more forward.

674
00:27:24,482 --> 00:27:25,811
(His body is in the best condition.)

675
00:27:25,812 --> 00:27:27,112
(He's done warming up for the next season.)

676
00:27:27,882 --> 00:27:29,782
I think you have more strength today.

677
00:27:32,022 --> 00:27:34,792
(He drinks water after exercising.)

678
00:27:35,492 --> 00:27:36,822
It's hard to drink the right amount of water, right?

679
00:27:37,262 --> 00:27:38,691
- I've drunk 2L of water. - What?

680
00:27:38,692 --> 00:27:39,831
- I've drunk 2L of water. - Did he say 2L?

681
00:27:39,832 --> 00:27:40,992
You need to drink a lot of water.

682
00:27:42,332 --> 00:27:43,901
(He has drunk 2L of water in the morning.)

683
00:27:43,902 --> 00:27:45,632
He drinks a lot of water.

684
00:27:46,832 --> 00:27:49,341
Hey, Ju Won, in what year were you born?

685
00:27:49,342 --> 00:27:51,641
- Were you born in 2001? - I was born in 2002.

686
00:27:51,642 --> 00:27:53,072
He's seven years younger.

687
00:27:54,042 --> 00:27:55,171
- He's seven years younger. - Kim Ju Won.

688
00:27:55,172 --> 00:27:56,242
Yes.

689
00:27:56,882 --> 00:27:58,911
He hit a tie-making home run at the end of the ninth inning.

690
00:27:58,912 --> 00:27:59,912
At the end.

691
00:27:59,913 --> 00:28:01,652
We were losing to Japan.

692
00:28:02,052 --> 00:28:03,581
We had 2 outs at the end of the 9th inning.

693
00:28:03,582 --> 00:28:05,491
I had only heard of that situation.

694
00:28:05,492 --> 00:28:07,151
- Yes. - Did he hit a home run then?

695
00:28:07,152 --> 00:28:09,392
Japan's best closing pitcher was on the mound.

696
00:28:09,722 --> 00:28:11,322
He threw the ball well.

697
00:28:12,992 --> 00:28:14,792
He hit a home run.

698
00:28:16,002 --> 00:28:17,201
- Tokyo. - It happened in Tokyo.

699
00:28:17,202 --> 00:28:19,272
He created silence in Tokyo. Complete silence.

700
00:28:20,932 --> 00:28:22,141
(Japan: 7, Korea: 7)

701
00:28:22,142 --> 00:28:23,501
When Ha Seong isn't around,

702
00:28:23,502 --> 00:28:26,341
Ju Won is the shortstop in the national team.

703
00:28:26,342 --> 00:28:28,311
- He has the same position. - The same position.

704
00:28:28,312 --> 00:28:29,742
Yes, he has the same position.

705
00:28:30,012 --> 00:28:33,051
Then you must be Ju Won's role model.

706
00:28:33,052 --> 00:28:34,052
That's right.

707
00:28:34,053 --> 00:28:36,981
- Well, he never told me that. - Didn't he tell you that?

708
00:28:36,982 --> 00:28:39,691
- But I think he respects me. - Of course.

709
00:28:39,692 --> 00:28:42,021
- I'm sure he does. - It's hard to say that...

710
00:28:42,022 --> 00:28:43,522
to your actual role model.

711
00:28:43,722 --> 00:28:45,362
You're right. I think I've told many lies.

712
00:28:45,632 --> 00:28:46,691
Did you have a role model?

713
00:28:46,692 --> 00:28:48,161
I always say that it's Son Pum Soo.

714
00:28:48,162 --> 00:28:50,762
(Joking)

715
00:28:51,602 --> 00:28:53,102
- Come on. - We're close.

716
00:28:53,572 --> 00:28:54,772
He's seven years younger.

717
00:28:55,402 --> 00:28:56,502
That's incredible.

718
00:28:57,302 --> 00:28:58,642
The future of Korean baseball...

719
00:28:59,812 --> 00:29:01,042
is bright.

720
00:29:02,812 --> 00:29:04,812
All done.

721
00:29:06,882 --> 00:29:08,782
Do you exercise like that every day?

722
00:29:09,082 --> 00:29:10,482
Yes. Except on weekends.

723
00:29:12,452 --> 00:29:16,492
(He walks somewhere after exercising.)

724
00:29:18,862 --> 00:29:23,501
(He enters a place.)

725
00:29:23,502 --> 00:29:25,771
- Tuna and fried tofu skin. - He's buying gimbap.

726
00:29:25,772 --> 00:29:27,172
(Tuna and fried tofu skin)

727
00:29:27,732 --> 00:29:29,171
He chose gimbap with a lot of protein.

728
00:29:29,172 --> 00:29:30,502
(He purchases gimbap for lunch after exercising.)

729
00:29:30,772 --> 00:29:32,872
- Tuna and fried tofu gimbap. - Thank you.

730
00:29:33,872 --> 00:29:37,112
(He goes somewhere after buying a roll of gimbap.)

731
00:29:37,982 --> 00:29:39,151
Mr. Kim Ha Seong,

732
00:29:39,152 --> 00:29:40,911
- would you take a selfie with me? - Sure.

733
00:29:40,912 --> 00:29:41,912
Thank you.

734
00:29:42,452 --> 00:29:45,051
My mom is a big fan.

735
00:29:45,052 --> 00:29:47,051
- His mom? - His mom?

736
00:29:47,052 --> 00:29:48,991
I think it came out wrong because he was so startled.

737
00:29:48,992 --> 00:29:49,992
- He went overboard. - Yes.

738
00:29:49,993 --> 00:29:51,022
One, two, three.

739
00:29:51,122 --> 00:29:52,391
(He takes a selfie with his mom's bias.)

740
00:29:52,392 --> 00:29:53,762
- Please be healthy. - Okay.

741
00:29:54,132 --> 00:29:56,131
(Please be healthy!)

742
00:29:56,132 --> 00:29:57,462
He was nervous.

743
00:29:58,032 --> 00:29:59,571
- He was nervous for real. - Seriously.

744
00:29:59,572 --> 00:30:01,032
He must be a big fan.

745
00:30:02,742 --> 00:30:04,571
(Holding a roll of gimbap, he gets into the car.)

746
00:30:04,572 --> 00:30:06,142
Gimbap and Bentley.

747
00:30:06,612 --> 00:30:07,671
It's cold.

748
00:30:07,672 --> 00:30:09,312
- Gimbap and Bentley. - It's a new combination.

749
00:30:10,082 --> 00:30:11,181
It looks different.

750
00:30:11,182 --> 00:30:13,051
- I bet it tastes good in a Bentley. - I know.

751
00:30:13,052 --> 00:30:14,752
(Grabbing)

752
00:30:17,452 --> 00:30:20,422
(Eating gimbap)

753
00:30:20,752 --> 00:30:22,922
(Chewing)

754
00:30:23,622 --> 00:30:26,662
(After eating a piece of gimbap, he drives somewhere.)

755
00:30:27,362 --> 00:30:30,702
(His car gets caught in a red light.)

756
00:30:31,032 --> 00:30:33,272
(Grabbing)

757
00:30:35,602 --> 00:30:37,741
(Inhaling)

758
00:30:37,742 --> 00:30:39,012
He must've been hungry.

759
00:30:39,312 --> 00:30:41,972
- He ate too little for breakfast. - He ate too little.

760
00:30:42,182 --> 00:30:44,641
(The major leaguer eats a roll of gimbap as a meal.)

761
00:30:44,642 --> 00:30:45,981
He likes ballad songs.

762
00:30:45,982 --> 00:30:47,882
(The car stops again.)

763
00:30:48,982 --> 00:30:51,022
(Grabbing again)

764
00:30:51,982 --> 00:30:54,822
(Eating again)

765
00:30:55,492 --> 00:30:57,892
(Stopping once again)

766
00:30:58,192 --> 00:30:59,491
(Eating once again)

767
00:30:59,492 --> 00:31:00,662
He's eating in a hurry.

768
00:31:01,432 --> 00:31:02,832
He must welcome the heavy traffic.

769
00:31:04,062 --> 00:31:06,732
(Thanks to the heavy traffic, he finishes eating inside the car.)

770
00:31:07,002 --> 00:31:09,142
(Grabbing)

771
00:31:10,342 --> 00:31:13,311
(He wraps by drinking water.)

772
00:31:13,312 --> 00:31:15,212
- He's drinking water again. - The bottle doesn't run out of it.

773
00:31:15,912 --> 00:31:18,212
Why do you drink so much water?

774
00:31:18,582 --> 00:31:19,812
Well, water...

775
00:31:21,112 --> 00:31:24,181
(Why does a major leaguer drink so much water?)

776
00:31:24,182 --> 00:31:25,252
(Gulping)

777
00:31:26,252 --> 00:31:27,722
is good for the body.

778
00:31:28,292 --> 00:31:30,161
(I see.)

779
00:31:30,162 --> 00:31:31,522
(Chuckling)

780
00:31:31,792 --> 00:31:33,762
We're getting so many no-nonsense answers today.

781
00:31:33,992 --> 00:31:36,831
I thought a major leaguer would have a special reason.

782
00:31:36,832 --> 00:31:38,631
I thought it was a different type of water.

783
00:31:38,632 --> 00:31:40,501
- We had a fantasy. - That's right.

784
00:31:40,502 --> 00:31:41,972
I expected a scientific reason.

785
00:31:42,672 --> 00:31:44,242
I'll drink some water.

786
00:31:44,642 --> 00:31:46,412
(Everyone drinks water.)

787
00:31:46,742 --> 00:31:50,212
(He sings as he drives.)

788
00:31:50,512 --> 00:31:53,612
(The major leaguer became happy after eating a roll of gimbap.)

789
00:31:54,552 --> 00:31:56,052
His singing skills are...

790
00:31:56,552 --> 00:31:58,991
enough to pass the phone interview of an audition show.

791
00:31:58,992 --> 00:32:00,522
- He'll pass the preliminaries. - That's right.

792
00:32:01,592 --> 00:32:04,292
(He arrives at a parking lot.)

793
00:32:04,962 --> 00:32:06,692
(Opening)

794
00:32:07,862 --> 00:32:08,901
- A bat? - What? It's a bat.

795
00:32:08,902 --> 00:32:10,502
- What? - Will he practice batting?

796
00:32:11,132 --> 00:32:15,672
(He enters a building with a baseball bat.)

797
00:32:17,072 --> 00:32:22,412
(Ha Seong arrives at a place with grass on the floor.)

798
00:32:24,242 --> 00:32:25,811
(It's a training center for baseball techniques.)

799
00:32:25,812 --> 00:32:29,552
It's where I go to train baseball techniques.

800
00:32:29,952 --> 00:32:31,482
He's Coach Jeong Gi Hun.

801
00:32:31,852 --> 00:32:34,622
We've been friends for about 12 years.

802
00:32:35,022 --> 00:32:37,662
We met on an 18U baseball team back in high school.

803
00:32:38,122 --> 00:32:40,262
Whenever I come to Korea during the off-season,

804
00:32:40,362 --> 00:32:42,702
he helps me exercise...

805
00:32:42,832 --> 00:32:44,301
and gives me feedback.

806
00:32:44,302 --> 00:32:45,902
We stay close.

807
00:32:46,232 --> 00:32:47,531
Did he retire?

808
00:32:47,532 --> 00:32:48,801
- Yes. - He retired.

809
00:32:48,802 --> 00:32:50,771
- He retired. - He became a coach.

810
00:32:50,772 --> 00:32:52,841
- Now, - He works as a coach.

811
00:32:52,842 --> 00:32:54,441
he works as a coach.

812
00:32:54,442 --> 00:32:57,781
My main coach who trains me for batting...

813
00:32:57,782 --> 00:32:59,152
is in the US.

814
00:32:59,912 --> 00:33:02,452
But Gi Hun went to US...

815
00:33:02,682 --> 00:33:04,752
and learned from my main coach.

816
00:33:05,452 --> 00:33:07,151
- Then he came to Korea. - That's right.

817
00:33:07,152 --> 00:33:09,021
Thus, their batting mechanisms...

818
00:33:09,022 --> 00:33:11,992
are about the same.

819
00:33:12,432 --> 00:33:15,532
That's why he gives me advice.

820
00:33:16,032 --> 00:33:19,632
- He put a lot of effort into it. - We came up with this arrangement.

821
00:33:20,132 --> 00:33:23,372
(Ha Seong is here to receive advice today as well.)

822
00:33:24,342 --> 00:33:26,942
(He puts on the glove and gets ready for training.)

823
00:33:28,272 --> 00:33:29,841
- Are your hands okay? - Yes.

824
00:33:29,842 --> 00:33:30,881
Don't you need to put on a glove?

825
00:33:30,882 --> 00:33:32,411
Is that catching training?

826
00:33:32,412 --> 00:33:34,712
Yes. It's a part of the routine.

827
00:33:36,681 --> 00:33:39,281
(Training for catching a ground ball)

828
00:33:41,203 --> 00:33:42,272
Four.

829
00:33:42,273 --> 00:33:43,372
(He catches the low ground balls.)

830
00:33:43,373 --> 00:33:44,443
Five.

831
00:33:47,756 --> 00:33:48,925
(He misses the ball.)

832
00:33:48,926 --> 00:33:49,966
It's a miss.

833
00:33:50,626 --> 00:33:51,696
Focus.

834
00:33:52,466 --> 00:33:53,996
- Let's focus. - What?

835
00:33:54,166 --> 00:33:55,196
Focus.

836
00:33:55,506 --> 00:33:57,766
- A friend can do that. - That's right.

837
00:33:58,206 --> 00:34:00,136
(He changes his pose.)

838
00:34:00,736 --> 00:34:01,775
One.

839
00:34:01,776 --> 00:34:02,975
(He catches the ground balls in a different pose.)

840
00:34:02,976 --> 00:34:04,906
Two. All right.

841
00:34:05,476 --> 00:34:06,915
Three.

842
00:34:06,916 --> 00:34:08,346
(The best friends turn serious during training.)

843
00:34:08,986 --> 00:34:13,116
You try catching the ball in a pose you'd be in during the game, right?

844
00:34:14,116 --> 00:34:15,656
Well, it isn't like that.

845
00:34:16,026 --> 00:34:18,255
- It's just a warmup. - It's just a routine.

846
00:34:18,256 --> 00:34:20,655
- It's just a routine. - Right.

847
00:34:20,656 --> 00:34:21,695
Yes.

848
00:34:21,696 --> 00:34:23,296
- "Right." - One out?

849
00:34:23,726 --> 00:34:26,296
"Right" is an original reaction.

850
00:34:27,066 --> 00:34:28,796
"Right."

851
00:34:30,266 --> 00:34:32,065
(He moves on to the next training.)

852
00:34:32,066 --> 00:34:33,136
Okay.

853
00:34:34,206 --> 00:34:36,076
(When the coach hits a ball with the bat,)

854
00:34:36,346 --> 00:34:38,005
(Ha Seong catches it and throws it back.)

855
00:34:38,006 --> 00:34:39,116
Okay.

856
00:34:40,076 --> 00:34:42,986
(The movement comes in handy during the infield defense.)

857
00:34:43,486 --> 00:34:46,215
Seriously, it's so elegant.

858
00:34:46,216 --> 00:34:48,285
Despite being the second baseman, he goes to the shortstop's area.

859
00:34:48,286 --> 00:34:49,825
The second baseman in the shortstop's area.

860
00:34:49,826 --> 00:34:51,555
That means he was fast.

861
00:34:51,556 --> 00:34:53,853
- That's right. - It's so elegant.

862
00:34:54,644 --> 00:34:55,703
(The coach who jokes around turns serious during training.)

863
00:34:55,704 --> 00:34:58,074
- Return the Golden Glove Award. - What was that?

864
00:34:58,244 --> 00:34:59,273
Return it.

865
00:34:59,274 --> 00:35:00,914
(Let's focus.)

866
00:35:02,544 --> 00:35:03,914
(Rolling)

867
00:35:04,914 --> 00:35:06,154
He missed another one.

868
00:35:08,924 --> 00:35:10,623
(Glaring)

869
00:35:10,624 --> 00:35:12,093
It's because it's a Korean ball.

870
00:35:12,094 --> 00:35:14,123
People praise you too much, but...

871
00:35:14,124 --> 00:35:15,264
It's because it's a Korean ball.

872
00:35:15,624 --> 00:35:17,034
Then use an American ball.

873
00:35:17,294 --> 00:35:19,264
- There's an American ball inside. - This is Korean grass.

874
00:35:19,734 --> 00:35:21,564
You have too many excuses. Go.

875
00:35:22,504 --> 00:35:24,573
(Nervous)

876
00:35:24,574 --> 00:35:25,704
Don't blame the tools.

877
00:35:27,244 --> 00:35:28,304
Backhand.

878
00:35:29,744 --> 00:35:30,813
Backhand.

879
00:35:30,814 --> 00:35:32,014
(It goes between his legs.)

880
00:35:33,074 --> 00:35:34,314
It's dangerous.

881
00:35:35,114 --> 00:35:36,813
This ground is bad.

882
00:35:36,814 --> 00:35:39,114
Don't say nonsense like that.

883
00:35:39,454 --> 00:35:40,454
(He adjusts to the bad ground.)

884
00:35:40,455 --> 00:35:41,554
This ground is bad.

885
00:35:42,224 --> 00:35:44,554
(His facial expression turns serious.)

886
00:35:46,024 --> 00:35:47,364
Good. There you go.

887
00:35:47,724 --> 00:35:49,263
- Nice. - Good.

888
00:35:49,264 --> 00:35:50,264
(Come on!)

889
00:35:51,894 --> 00:35:53,033
That's a really hard one.

890
00:35:53,034 --> 00:35:55,633
It looks easy, but it's very hard.

891
00:35:55,634 --> 00:35:56,664
Let's stop.

892
00:35:57,604 --> 00:35:58,674
Are you exhausted?

893
00:35:59,774 --> 00:36:02,574
(Panting)

894
00:36:02,844 --> 00:36:04,443
(The coach sets up a camera.)

895
00:36:04,444 --> 00:36:05,474
What?

896
00:36:05,574 --> 00:36:07,943
(Ha Seong is on the screen.)

897
00:36:07,944 --> 00:36:09,944
I guess there's a machine for analysis.

898
00:36:10,614 --> 00:36:11,884
- Three. - Okay.

899
00:36:15,824 --> 00:36:16,824
(Hitting)

900
00:36:17,024 --> 00:36:18,024
(Hitting)

901
00:36:18,025 --> 00:36:19,094
My goodness.

902
00:36:19,524 --> 00:36:20,593
There you go.

903
00:36:20,594 --> 00:36:22,063
The hits are so strong.

904
00:36:22,064 --> 00:36:24,434
(His batting form gets filmed on the monitor.)

905
00:36:25,694 --> 00:36:28,833
(He puts a bar in the middle of the batter's box.)

906
00:36:28,834 --> 00:36:30,974
Is it a part of the routine? What kind of training is this?

907
00:36:31,304 --> 00:36:32,334
It's the batting training.

908
00:36:32,634 --> 00:36:35,173
(Panting)

909
00:36:35,174 --> 00:36:36,274
He's panting already.

910
00:36:36,474 --> 00:36:37,714
Aren't you resting for too long?

911
00:36:38,774 --> 00:36:40,344
You hit one ball and rest.

912
00:36:40,914 --> 00:36:44,014
(He pretends not to hear his coach.)

913
00:36:44,114 --> 00:36:45,414
Hurry up and do it.

914
00:36:46,154 --> 00:36:48,283
(He hits the ball again.)

915
00:36:48,284 --> 00:36:49,324
Okay.

916
00:36:49,924 --> 00:36:50,924
(Hitting)

917
00:36:51,154 --> 00:36:52,424
The sound changed.

918
00:36:53,424 --> 00:36:55,024
How does he hit it like that?

919
00:36:57,934 --> 00:36:59,993
(He hits it like this.)

920
00:36:59,994 --> 00:37:01,334
- It sounds like a gun. - Okay.

921
00:37:02,804 --> 00:37:04,534
- His swing is so satisfying. - Nice.

922
00:37:04,634 --> 00:37:06,704
- He doesn't even rest. - He hit the ball well just now.

923
00:37:07,004 --> 00:37:08,143
That was great.

924
00:37:08,144 --> 00:37:09,144
(I'll monitor my performance.)

925
00:37:09,474 --> 00:37:10,573
(Let's see.)

926
00:37:10,574 --> 00:37:12,344
- He'll monitor his performance. - His batting form.

927
00:37:12,814 --> 00:37:16,443
You stride forward during the game, but...

928
00:37:16,444 --> 00:37:18,153
- The distance between the legs? - Yes.

929
00:37:18,154 --> 00:37:19,254
(That's what he means by a stride.)

930
00:37:19,754 --> 00:37:22,354
I'm sure the physicality is different,

931
00:37:22,484 --> 00:37:25,453
but there's a difference of 10 to 20 degrees.

932
00:37:25,454 --> 00:37:28,464
I think you can move forward more and split your legs more.

933
00:37:30,894 --> 00:37:32,064
Do you agree with that?

934
00:37:32,294 --> 00:37:33,833
- Do you agree with that? - No.

935
00:37:33,834 --> 00:37:35,204
Isn't it because of his big build?

936
00:37:35,964 --> 00:37:38,934
After I moved from Korea to the US,

937
00:37:39,134 --> 00:37:40,543
I changed my batting form...

938
00:37:40,544 --> 00:37:41,903
- little by little. - That's right. You changed it.

939
00:37:41,904 --> 00:37:45,474
Even though I work in the US,

940
00:37:45,644 --> 00:37:48,684
many people give me advice.

941
00:37:48,984 --> 00:37:50,954
I accept them with gratitude.

942
00:37:51,184 --> 00:37:54,884
I agreed with what he said about my stride.

943
00:37:55,354 --> 00:37:57,324
I agreed that I needed to step forward more.

944
00:37:57,494 --> 00:37:58,723
- You needed to step forward - When you hit the ball?

945
00:37:58,724 --> 00:38:02,724
I really didn't move forward when I hit the ball.

946
00:38:02,824 --> 00:38:04,133
- You stayed still. - Yes.

947
00:38:04,134 --> 00:38:06,694
- I agreed with that. - It helped.

948
00:38:06,864 --> 00:38:08,803
He gives me such key points.

949
00:38:08,804 --> 00:38:10,473
I bet you're saying this because you felt bad.

950
00:38:10,474 --> 00:38:13,134
(Seeing how you're talking about it)

951
00:38:13,604 --> 00:38:15,004
Increase the number little at a time.

952
00:38:15,704 --> 00:38:17,914
You should hit the right number of balls.

953
00:38:19,174 --> 00:38:20,274
You need to decide the number.

954
00:38:21,284 --> 00:38:24,554
(He cleans up after practice right away.)

955
00:38:25,684 --> 00:38:28,124
(He picks up 4 balls with 1 hand.)

956
00:38:29,024 --> 00:38:34,223
(He cleans up fast with his big hands.)

957
00:38:34,224 --> 00:38:35,794
Earlier, I saw...

958
00:38:36,164 --> 00:38:39,164
that baseball players had calluses in this part of their hands.

959
00:38:39,364 --> 00:38:40,864
Is it because of the bat?

960
00:38:41,064 --> 00:38:43,364
- Yes. Here. - Look.

961
00:38:43,634 --> 00:38:45,474
- I've never seen calluses here. - I know.

962
00:38:45,674 --> 00:38:48,104
- You're right. - He has calluses here.

963
00:38:49,304 --> 00:38:51,214
He has calluses here.

964
00:38:51,374 --> 00:38:52,844
- I see. - Let me see them.

965
00:38:52,944 --> 00:38:54,284
It's raised.

966
00:38:55,544 --> 00:38:56,584
(Proud)

967
00:38:56,784 --> 00:38:58,054
It's like my mom's foot.

968
00:38:59,854 --> 00:39:01,824
- Why would you say that? - You're such a bad son.

969
00:39:02,224 --> 00:39:03,353
Are your mom's feet that hard?

970
00:39:03,354 --> 00:39:04,694
(Fidgeting)

971
00:39:04,894 --> 00:39:05,953
I'm going now.

972
00:39:05,954 --> 00:39:08,964
(With his tiger-like coach who is also his best friend,)

973
00:39:09,094 --> 00:39:11,064
(he had an hour-long technique training.)

974
00:39:12,964 --> 00:39:16,664
(Ha Seong goes somewhere again.)

975
00:39:18,104 --> 00:39:19,403
- Is it a supermarket? - It's a supermarket.

976
00:39:19,404 --> 00:39:20,504
It's a supermarket.

977
00:39:24,214 --> 00:39:25,974
Maybe he'll get all the chicken breasts.

978
00:39:26,274 --> 00:39:28,584
I think he'll eat pork and beef.

979
00:39:29,084 --> 00:39:30,144
It must be here.

980
00:39:32,054 --> 00:39:33,153
Cucumbers.

981
00:39:33,154 --> 00:39:34,583
(He puts a bag of cucumbers in his cart.)

982
00:39:34,584 --> 00:39:35,624
Cucumbers.

983
00:39:37,354 --> 00:39:38,954
He's buying unpeeled onions.

984
00:39:43,264 --> 00:39:44,533
(He gets ingredients without hesitation.)

985
00:39:44,534 --> 00:39:45,664
What will he cook?

986
00:39:47,804 --> 00:39:49,534
(He stops his cart in front of Korean beef.)

987
00:39:49,764 --> 00:39:52,374
Thin flank.

988
00:39:53,674 --> 00:39:56,674
(Picking up)

989
00:40:00,944 --> 00:40:02,184
Six packs for one person?

990
00:40:03,344 --> 00:40:04,753
I bet he eats a lot.

991
00:40:04,754 --> 00:40:05,854
I bet he does.

992
00:40:08,654 --> 00:40:10,324
(He finishes paying.)

993
00:40:12,794 --> 00:40:13,794
It's hot.

994
00:40:18,164 --> 00:40:19,234
My goodness.

995
00:40:29,604 --> 00:40:31,774
(He puts the bag on the table.)

996
00:40:31,944 --> 00:40:33,314
(He brings the clothing bag to the bedroom.)

997
00:40:37,654 --> 00:40:39,554
(Rummaging)

998
00:40:47,124 --> 00:40:48,394
- What is he doing? - What is that?

999
00:40:49,324 --> 00:40:51,094
- Salt? - Yes, it's salt.

1000
00:40:51,894 --> 00:40:53,664
- Salt? - Why are you doing that?

1001
00:40:53,764 --> 00:40:55,533
I was told to wash it like that.

1002
00:40:55,534 --> 00:40:57,734
- Did your mom tell you that? - Yes. So I just do that.

1003
00:41:00,744 --> 00:41:03,604
(His muscles bulge.)

1004
00:41:08,284 --> 00:41:09,843
(He shakes off the water with his forearm muscles...)

1005
00:41:09,844 --> 00:41:11,384
(that brought him the Golden Glove Award.)

1006
00:41:14,784 --> 00:41:16,284
(Focused)

1007
00:41:16,984 --> 00:41:18,794
(He scores the inside...)

1008
00:41:19,454 --> 00:41:21,223
(to remove the seeds with precision.)

1009
00:41:21,224 --> 00:41:23,024
Why do you remove the seeds? Do you not like them?

1010
00:41:23,064 --> 00:41:26,063
If I keep the seeds, the dish turns watery.

1011
00:41:26,064 --> 00:41:27,804
- Because it turns watery? - Yes.

1012
00:41:28,104 --> 00:41:29,164
There we go.

1013
00:41:29,204 --> 00:41:31,174
(He finishes preparing cucumbers.)

1014
00:41:32,534 --> 00:41:34,604
(He prepares an onion as well.)

1015
00:41:37,974 --> 00:41:41,984
I see that you cook for yourself.

1016
00:41:43,014 --> 00:41:46,453
I enjoy cooking. I think it's fun.

1017
00:41:46,454 --> 00:41:47,923
- Really? - Do you cook?

1018
00:41:47,924 --> 00:41:49,653
Do you cook in the US?

1019
00:41:49,654 --> 00:41:50,754
Yes.

1020
00:41:51,294 --> 00:41:52,994
I love Korean food a lot.

1021
00:41:54,494 --> 00:41:56,894
(Pouring)

1022
00:41:58,894 --> 00:42:00,333
(He adds different ingredients to gochujang with ease.)

1023
00:42:00,334 --> 00:42:02,804
Minced garlic, chili powder, gochujang...

1024
00:42:04,134 --> 00:42:05,534
(Sniffing)

1025
00:42:07,334 --> 00:42:08,844
- It looks tasty. - That's ready.

1026
00:42:12,614 --> 00:42:14,144
He adds the whelk soup.

1027
00:42:15,314 --> 00:42:17,414
(He adds all the solid ingredients.)

1028
00:42:18,854 --> 00:42:20,554
(It's time to mix.)

1029
00:42:21,154 --> 00:42:23,553
With the hands that won the Gold Glove Award...

1030
00:42:23,554 --> 00:42:24,724
The golden whelks.

1031
00:42:26,924 --> 00:42:29,263
(I'll give the world-class mixing.)

1032
00:42:29,264 --> 00:42:30,564
My goodness.

1033
00:42:31,094 --> 00:42:32,494
The whelks look delicious.

1034
00:42:41,004 --> 00:42:43,273
(This is the taste.)

1035
00:42:43,274 --> 00:42:44,744
It looks tasty.

1036
00:42:46,314 --> 00:42:48,714
(He adds the ingredients as he sees fit.)

1037
00:42:49,184 --> 00:42:51,354
He must be used to cooking.

1038
00:42:51,714 --> 00:42:53,314
(He makes eyeball measurements.)

1039
00:42:54,724 --> 00:42:57,694
(He pours bone broth.)

1040
00:43:00,224 --> 00:43:01,464
(It smells good.)

1041
00:43:06,864 --> 00:43:08,364
Someone is coming.

1042
00:43:08,504 --> 00:43:09,803
He isn't eating alone.

1043
00:43:09,804 --> 00:43:11,373
(Who came to Ha Seong's place?)

1044
00:43:11,374 --> 00:43:12,374
Who is it?

1045
00:43:13,032 --> 00:43:15,271
(Ha Seong is cooking alone.)

1046
00:43:15,272 --> 00:43:16,771
Someone is coming.

1047
00:43:16,772 --> 00:43:18,302
He isn't eating alone.

1048
00:43:19,472 --> 00:43:20,572
Who is it?

1049
00:43:22,042 --> 00:43:23,271
(Two people punch in the password and walk in.)

1050
00:43:23,272 --> 00:43:24,782
- There is another one. - There are two people.

1051
00:43:28,252 --> 00:43:29,312
What's up?

1052
00:43:29,512 --> 00:43:32,022
- Did they punch in the password? - What's up, dude?

1053
00:43:32,082 --> 00:43:34,192
Yes, they know the password.

1054
00:43:35,392 --> 00:43:37,392
- What are you doing? - Why did you come back?

1055
00:43:37,592 --> 00:43:39,221
- We saw each other earlier. - It's the friend we saw earlier.

1056
00:43:39,222 --> 00:43:40,962
You're right. The friend who's a coach.

1057
00:43:41,862 --> 00:43:44,462
(The tiger-like coach didn't allow the smallest mistake.)

1058
00:43:45,432 --> 00:43:46,432
(Gi Hun is a best friend who trains and eats with him.)

1059
00:43:46,433 --> 00:43:47,732
- He's a best friend. - Do you need help?

1060
00:43:48,672 --> 00:43:50,432
(Another friend has come with Gi Hun.)

1061
00:43:51,072 --> 00:43:52,741
- Who said it was fine? - Run!

1062
00:43:52,742 --> 00:43:54,001
The second base.

1063
00:43:54,002 --> 00:43:55,471
He gets taken out at the second base.

1064
00:43:55,472 --> 00:43:58,211
I see. He's Kim Jae Hyun.

1065
00:43:58,212 --> 00:43:59,242
Yes.

1066
00:43:59,312 --> 00:44:00,441
(Kim Jae Hyun, Kim Ha Seong)

1067
00:44:00,442 --> 00:44:02,311
- Is that you? - That's right.

1068
00:44:02,312 --> 00:44:03,452
They were on the same team.

1069
00:44:04,522 --> 00:44:09,022
(The three of them became close through baseball.)

1070
00:44:11,692 --> 00:44:13,061
So, are you hungry?

1071
00:44:13,062 --> 00:44:14,191
I'm hungry.

1072
00:44:14,192 --> 00:44:15,392
I'm about to die.

1073
00:44:15,992 --> 00:44:17,032
Did you see that?

1074
00:44:17,662 --> 00:44:18,662
Yes.

1075
00:44:19,632 --> 00:44:20,732
It's wearing clothes too.

1076
00:44:22,172 --> 00:44:24,342
(Fascinated)

1077
00:44:24,842 --> 00:44:26,702
- Have you seen it before? - It's my first time.

1078
00:44:28,812 --> 00:44:30,141
It resembles you a bit.

1079
00:44:30,142 --> 00:44:31,182
(Taking out)

1080
00:44:31,612 --> 00:44:33,311
- I need to be paler for that. - Wilson.

1081
00:44:33,312 --> 00:44:34,712
(He takes out water and drinks it naturally.)

1082
00:44:35,382 --> 00:44:38,582
(He walks over somewhere.)

1083
00:44:39,552 --> 00:44:41,152
How many Cheongyang peppers should I add?

1084
00:44:41,352 --> 00:44:42,751
Three? Two?

1085
00:44:42,752 --> 00:44:43,991
(He enters the dressing room.)

1086
00:44:43,992 --> 00:44:46,122
- Two. - Two.

1087
00:44:46,722 --> 00:44:47,991
They have the best friends' vibes.

1088
00:44:47,992 --> 00:44:50,192
He even wanders around the house. It's perfect.

1089
00:44:50,662 --> 00:44:52,062
Shall I add one more Cheongyang pepper?

1090
00:44:52,362 --> 00:44:53,601
You're going to add it anyway.

1091
00:44:53,602 --> 00:44:55,102
I forgot to buy tofu.

1092
00:44:55,272 --> 00:44:56,832
What else did you add? MSG?

1093
00:44:57,032 --> 00:44:59,241
- I'm not going to add it. - You always add it.

1094
00:44:59,242 --> 00:45:00,302
What are you saying?

1095
00:45:01,612 --> 00:45:04,142
Isn't this security camera footage?

1096
00:45:05,312 --> 00:45:06,381
There's no meaning.

1097
00:45:06,382 --> 00:45:07,481
(Embarrassed)

1098
00:45:07,482 --> 00:45:09,911
- There are no pleasantries. - There are no pleasantries.

1099
00:45:09,912 --> 00:45:11,152
They just say what they want to say.

1100
00:45:11,352 --> 00:45:12,581
I love it.

1101
00:45:12,582 --> 00:45:14,492
- It's like security camera footage. - I love it.

1102
00:45:14,992 --> 00:45:17,022
Hey, get ready to eat now.

1103
00:45:17,152 --> 00:45:18,392
- Do you need help? - What?

1104
00:45:18,762 --> 00:45:20,122
- Do you need help? - Get ready to eat.

1105
00:45:20,422 --> 00:45:21,961
(What do I need to do?)

1106
00:45:21,962 --> 00:45:22,992
What is it?

1107
00:45:23,762 --> 00:45:25,531
- Where is it? - Come here.

1108
00:45:25,532 --> 00:45:27,202
I want you to do this.

1109
00:45:27,932 --> 00:45:29,631
(He readily walks over to help.)

1110
00:45:29,632 --> 00:45:30,672
Shall I mix everything?

1111
00:45:33,442 --> 00:45:37,042
(He mixes everything without a complaint.)

1112
00:45:37,682 --> 00:45:38,912
I need a trivet under the soup.

1113
00:45:40,182 --> 00:45:41,812
(He prepares it right away.)

1114
00:45:42,112 --> 00:45:43,682
Shall we scoop some out on our plates?

1115
00:45:43,852 --> 00:45:45,682
Scoop out the amount you want.

1116
00:45:46,682 --> 00:45:47,692
There's a lot.

1117
00:45:48,652 --> 00:45:50,121
(The tiger-like coach has become a docile sheep.)

1118
00:45:50,122 --> 00:45:52,321
At home, he's just a friend. He isn't a coach.

1119
00:45:52,322 --> 00:45:53,322
That's right.

1120
00:45:53,822 --> 00:45:56,262
(Thanks to the friends' help)

1121
00:45:57,632 --> 00:45:58,801
You made a lot of food.

1122
00:45:58,802 --> 00:46:00,062
- I'll start grilling meat now. - Okay.

1123
00:46:02,002 --> 00:46:03,401
That kimchi jjigae looks tasty.

1124
00:46:03,402 --> 00:46:04,972
The color of the kimchi jjigae tells me that it's tasty.

1125
00:46:06,102 --> 00:46:08,542
(Beef will fill their stomachs.)

1126
00:46:09,672 --> 00:46:11,381
- It looks tasty. - Whelks.

1127
00:46:11,382 --> 00:46:12,582
Whelks look tasty.

1128
00:46:12,742 --> 00:46:15,152
(Ha Seong's Korean meal is complete.)

1129
00:46:17,482 --> 00:46:18,722
Eat up.

1130
00:46:19,952 --> 00:46:22,192
(The man who cooked, Ha Seong, takes a bite first.)

1131
00:46:23,792 --> 00:46:25,562
(Humming in approval)

1132
00:46:27,492 --> 00:46:29,662
(He rips kimchi with his hands!)

1133
00:46:30,092 --> 00:46:31,102
(Sucking)

1134
00:46:31,932 --> 00:46:34,571
(He wraps white rice with it and stuffs his mouth.)

1135
00:46:34,572 --> 00:46:36,002
It must be tasty.

1136
00:46:38,372 --> 00:46:43,371
(His two friends eat without any words.)

1137
00:46:43,372 --> 00:46:44,482
There isn't a lot of meat.

1138
00:46:45,012 --> 00:46:46,082
They must've been hungry.

1139
00:46:47,112 --> 00:46:48,811
The one who cooked...

1140
00:46:48,812 --> 00:46:50,151
must be worried about their silence.

1141
00:46:50,152 --> 00:46:51,382
Yes.

1142
00:46:54,122 --> 00:46:55,192
- It's tasty. - It's tasty.

1143
00:46:56,792 --> 00:46:58,922
- It's hot. - The kimchi is nice.

1144
00:46:59,222 --> 00:47:00,292
It's tasty.

1145
00:47:01,932 --> 00:47:04,061
- The reactions are nice. - He pretends not to hear them.

1146
00:47:04,062 --> 00:47:05,562
It's high praise.

1147
00:47:06,562 --> 00:47:07,602
It's insanely hot.

1148
00:47:08,472 --> 00:47:09,932
Would you turn on the air conditioner?

1149
00:47:11,242 --> 00:47:12,801
It's hot. Would it be okay if I changed into new clothes?

1150
00:47:12,802 --> 00:47:14,172
It's a men's conversation.

1151
00:47:15,242 --> 00:47:16,512
The air conditioner is on.

1152
00:47:17,312 --> 00:47:19,181
- It's on. - Why are you wearing comfy clothes?

1153
00:47:19,182 --> 00:47:20,282
(Jae Hyun goes somewhere.)

1154
00:47:21,352 --> 00:47:22,752
Does it smell strongly of meat?

1155
00:47:23,112 --> 00:47:24,182
No.

1156
00:47:26,082 --> 00:47:27,222
It's nice.

1157
00:47:29,492 --> 00:47:30,822
- Is that my T-shirt? - Yes.

1158
00:47:30,992 --> 00:47:32,122
- Is that my T-shirt? - Yes.

1159
00:47:32,822 --> 00:47:34,991
Did you pick a white T-shirt to wear during the meal?

1160
00:47:34,992 --> 00:47:37,361
- Yes. I spotted it first. - Did you have to do that?

1161
00:47:37,362 --> 00:47:38,731
There are many black T-shirts.

1162
00:47:38,732 --> 00:47:40,131
No, there aren't. I didn't see them.

1163
00:47:40,132 --> 00:47:42,202
- Hey, come here. - He's going to change.

1164
00:47:42,672 --> 00:47:43,701
I need to change.

1165
00:47:43,702 --> 00:47:45,102
Hey, wear a black top.

1166
00:47:45,272 --> 00:47:46,272
Gi Hun.

1167
00:47:46,273 --> 00:47:48,272
If you pick an expensive one, you won't be able to wear it home.

1168
00:47:48,712 --> 00:47:50,242
(Dumbfounded)

1169
00:47:51,482 --> 00:47:53,212
- I found it. - He wore a white T-shirt.

1170
00:47:53,382 --> 00:47:55,812
(He wore a white T-shirt like Jae Hyun.)

1171
00:47:55,982 --> 00:47:58,051
- Of course. - He did it on purpose.

1172
00:47:58,052 --> 00:47:59,521
He should've worn new pants as well.

1173
00:47:59,522 --> 00:48:02,252
Food particles and oil are bound to get on...

1174
00:48:02,422 --> 00:48:03,452
the T-shirt.

1175
00:48:04,252 --> 00:48:06,922
(This is great.)

1176
00:48:07,362 --> 00:48:10,332
(He can't believe his eyes.)

1177
00:48:12,032 --> 00:48:13,332
Gi Hun, sprinkle some salt.

1178
00:48:14,302 --> 00:48:16,132
You haven't had surgery either, right?

1179
00:48:16,432 --> 00:48:17,842
In high school, I had one.

1180
00:48:20,572 --> 00:48:22,111
He had ankle surgery.

1181
00:48:22,112 --> 00:48:23,472
(Salt doesn't come out.)

1182
00:48:23,572 --> 00:48:25,342
Is it coming out? For goodness' sake.

1183
00:48:26,282 --> 00:48:27,852
(Timid)

1184
00:48:30,552 --> 00:48:31,982
- Am I doing it wrong? - Is it yours?

1185
00:48:32,182 --> 00:48:33,351
It's new.

1186
00:48:33,352 --> 00:48:34,352
(What?)

1187
00:48:34,852 --> 00:48:37,752
(Not knowing what's wrong, he keeps turning it.)

1188
00:48:38,392 --> 00:48:40,292
- Gosh. - Open it and remove the seal.

1189
00:48:41,792 --> 00:48:43,662
- Open it? - It's new, right?

1190
00:48:45,102 --> 00:48:46,632
- No way. - It has to be new.

1191
00:48:47,232 --> 00:48:49,972
(The opening is sealed.)

1192
00:48:51,472 --> 00:48:53,372
- Why are you so dumb? - You...

1193
00:48:54,872 --> 00:48:57,242
(Dying of laughter)

1194
00:48:57,912 --> 00:48:59,812
(Embarrassed)

1195
00:48:59,842 --> 00:49:01,952
When friends gather around,

1196
00:49:02,012 --> 00:49:03,651
the atmosphere stays the same...

1197
00:49:03,652 --> 00:49:05,151
whether the location is your house or a resort.

1198
00:49:05,152 --> 00:49:06,152
- You're right. - Right?

1199
00:49:06,153 --> 00:49:09,152
I find it so hilarious that they're at L Tower.

1200
00:49:09,822 --> 00:49:10,892
I thought that to myself as well.

1201
00:49:11,052 --> 00:49:12,861
- It's a guest house in Yangpyeong. - An Airbnb in Yangpyeong.

1202
00:49:12,862 --> 00:49:14,391
(It's a guest house in Yangpyeong.)

1203
00:49:14,392 --> 00:49:15,692
Right. It seems like it.

1204
00:49:15,932 --> 00:49:18,202
- It has to make a grinding sound. - It has to be opened first.

1205
00:49:18,862 --> 00:49:20,162
Are you sure?

1206
00:49:20,802 --> 00:49:22,172
It has to be opened first.

1207
00:49:22,572 --> 00:49:24,701
You were doing it confidently as if you knew how to use it.

1208
00:49:24,702 --> 00:49:27,172
I thought you were struggling to use it.

1209
00:49:28,342 --> 00:49:29,742
Gosh, I'm sweating all of a sudden.

1210
00:49:30,942 --> 00:49:33,882
Let's say you get...

1211
00:49:34,242 --> 00:49:36,952
a good offer right away tomorrow.

1212
00:49:38,182 --> 00:49:39,522
Do you have to head to the US right away?

1213
00:49:40,622 --> 00:49:41,652
Yes.

1214
00:49:41,922 --> 00:49:43,721
But I don't know what to do right now.

1215
00:49:43,722 --> 00:49:46,391
Do you have any thoughts about retiring in Korea?

1216
00:49:46,392 --> 00:49:47,422
I'm curious about that.

1217
00:49:49,032 --> 00:49:51,462
If Kiwoom Heroes asks me to come back?

1218
00:49:52,262 --> 00:49:53,462
What if they will ask you to come back no matter what?

1219
00:49:53,832 --> 00:49:54,932
Then I must come back.

1220
00:49:55,332 --> 00:49:57,601
Are you thinking about ending your career in Korea?

1221
00:49:57,602 --> 00:49:58,642
Yes.

1222
00:49:58,742 --> 00:49:59,871
Your seniors, Park Chan Ho and Kim Byung Hyun,

1223
00:49:59,872 --> 00:50:01,001
- did the same. - Right.

1224
00:50:01,002 --> 00:50:02,411
- They came back to Korea. - Ryu Hyun Jin.

1225
00:50:02,412 --> 00:50:04,071
Ryu Hyun Jin and Choo Shin Soo.

1226
00:50:04,072 --> 00:50:05,112
Right.

1227
00:50:05,542 --> 00:50:08,911
As I played for Kiwoon Heroes,

1228
00:50:08,912 --> 00:50:10,351
- I was able to make it to the US. - Right.

1229
00:50:10,352 --> 00:50:14,591
I want to play with them before I end my career.

1230
00:50:14,592 --> 00:50:15,952
(A heart of wanting to end his career with them out of gratitude)

1231
00:50:16,522 --> 00:50:17,992
I want to play with Ha Seong before my career ends.

1232
00:50:19,022 --> 00:50:20,762
We were on the same team for seven years.

1233
00:50:21,762 --> 00:50:23,691
But we weren't able to...

1234
00:50:23,692 --> 00:50:26,202
play together as much.

1235
00:50:26,602 --> 00:50:28,272
I just clapped from the dugout.

1236
00:50:28,932 --> 00:50:30,101
I must've done well...

1237
00:50:30,102 --> 00:50:31,742
- because you did that. - Right.

1238
00:50:32,772 --> 00:50:35,771
Jae Hyun was like a mentor to me starting from a young age.

1239
00:50:35,772 --> 00:50:37,112
He must have supported him a lot mentally.

1240
00:50:37,242 --> 00:50:38,712
(Peeking)

1241
00:50:39,312 --> 00:50:41,751
Still, Jae Hyun was in the same team with you.

1242
00:50:41,752 --> 00:50:42,881
(Feeling jealous)

1243
00:50:42,882 --> 00:50:44,682
You were jealous that we were on the same team, right?

1244
00:50:44,852 --> 00:50:46,421
- We were all together. - Right.

1245
00:50:46,422 --> 00:50:47,922
I was the only one to play for a different team.

1246
00:50:48,422 --> 00:50:49,851
I was the only one to play for a different team.

1247
00:50:49,852 --> 00:50:51,091
Ha Seong, Jae Hyun,

1248
00:50:51,092 --> 00:50:52,661
Ji Yeol, and Jung Hoo.

1249
00:50:52,662 --> 00:50:53,792
All four of you were on the same team.

1250
00:50:53,992 --> 00:50:56,062
Right. Why didn't you work hard?

1251
00:50:56,792 --> 00:50:57,862
He's getting at him.

1252
00:50:58,102 --> 00:50:59,431
That was why I went down to the reserves.

1253
00:50:59,432 --> 00:51:01,131
(He makes his response lightly.)

1254
00:51:01,132 --> 00:51:03,502
But after all that,

1255
00:51:03,802 --> 00:51:06,842
you're living a better second act of your life now.

1256
00:51:07,342 --> 00:51:08,571
So I'm saying...

1257
00:51:08,572 --> 00:51:10,111
- there's a time for everything. - There's a set schedule.

1258
00:51:10,112 --> 00:51:12,212
- Everyone has their moment. - Right. That's a great line.

1259
00:51:12,542 --> 00:51:13,681
I wouldn't have dreamt of becoming a coach...

1260
00:51:13,682 --> 00:51:14,852
if it wasn't for him.

1261
00:51:15,352 --> 00:51:16,581
- What would you have done? - I'm being honest.

1262
00:51:16,582 --> 00:51:19,082
After being released from the team,

1263
00:51:19,882 --> 00:51:21,322
I drank every single day.

1264
00:51:21,792 --> 00:51:23,721
I drank and cured my hangover over and over.

1265
00:51:23,722 --> 00:51:27,322
I contacted him one day.

1266
00:51:27,892 --> 00:51:30,761
It was the first year he went to the US.

1267
00:51:30,762 --> 00:51:33,262
- During my first year... - He had a hole in his head.

1268
00:51:33,662 --> 00:51:35,072
He lost so much hair.

1269
00:51:36,172 --> 00:51:37,972
I called him and said I was struggling.

1270
00:51:38,172 --> 00:51:40,372
Around 30 to 40 minutes later,

1271
00:51:40,942 --> 00:51:43,412
he sent me a plane ticket.

1272
00:51:44,072 --> 00:51:45,081
He said,

1273
00:51:45,082 --> 00:51:46,142
- "Come to the US tomorrow." - That's impressive.

1274
00:51:46,542 --> 00:51:48,752
The plane was scheduled to set off at 7pm the next day.

1275
00:51:49,152 --> 00:51:51,152
- That was the schedule. - He's so impressive.

1276
00:51:51,782 --> 00:51:54,051
He said, "Think that you're visiting Jeju Island for a week."

1277
00:51:54,052 --> 00:51:56,222
I just brought three pairs of shorts and T-shirts with me.

1278
00:51:56,492 --> 00:51:58,692
I extended my stay 3 times and stayed for 3 months.

1279
00:51:59,092 --> 00:52:00,521
I got rid of my clothes and borrowed his clothes...

1280
00:52:00,522 --> 00:52:01,692
to stay for three months.

1281
00:52:02,192 --> 00:52:03,792
Did you call him because you were bored?

1282
00:52:04,092 --> 00:52:05,701
- No. - No. I'm sure that wasn't it.

1283
00:52:05,702 --> 00:52:07,761
I felt so lonely,

1284
00:52:07,762 --> 00:52:09,031
and I struggled so much at that time.

1285
00:52:09,032 --> 00:52:10,732
So I just went,

1286
00:52:11,772 --> 00:52:13,141
"Let's not struggle separately."

1287
00:52:13,142 --> 00:52:14,372
"Let's struggle together."

1288
00:52:15,242 --> 00:52:18,412
I wasn't picked to play all the time as well,

1289
00:52:18,782 --> 00:52:21,212
so I asked him to come and talk with me.

1290
00:52:22,512 --> 00:52:23,682
Do you know what the important part is?

1291
00:52:24,052 --> 00:52:25,682
I was with him for around ten days.

1292
00:52:26,122 --> 00:52:27,882
He had to be away for two weeks for away games.

1293
00:52:28,052 --> 00:52:30,192
All he left with me was his credit card.

1294
00:52:30,522 --> 00:52:32,391
"Order food with this."

1295
00:52:32,392 --> 00:52:33,591
He took a plane and left after that.

1296
00:52:33,592 --> 00:52:36,292
I was left alone in San Diego just like that.

1297
00:52:36,932 --> 00:52:39,202
I didn't even know how to make an order at a restaurant.

1298
00:52:39,632 --> 00:52:41,061
That was how I stayed alone for two weeks.

1299
00:52:41,062 --> 00:52:43,332
(The true Korean waited for Ha Seong desperately for 2 weeks.)

1300
00:52:43,902 --> 00:52:45,442
I comforted him so much.

1301
00:52:45,772 --> 00:52:46,941
I truly did.

1302
00:52:46,942 --> 00:52:48,142
He said this.

1303
